---
import Guide from "../../../layouts/Guide.astro"
import CodeGroup from "../../../components/CodeGroup.astro"
import DocLink from "../../../components/DocLink.astro"
import Code from "../../../components/Code.astro"
import { pickAndChooseCss } from "../../../utils/getting-started"
---

<Guide overline="Guide">
  <Fragment slot="title">Getting started</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    OPUI ships first-class Astro components. Install the package, import what
    you need, and you're set.
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2 id="installation">Install via NPM</h2>

    <CodeGroup
      tabs={[
        {
          title: "pnpm",
          code: "pnpm add opui-css open-props astro -S",
          lang: "sh",
        },
        {
          title: "npm",
          code: "npm install opui-css open-props astro -S",
          lang: "sh",
        },
      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="css">Import the CSS</h2>
    <p>
      Astro components ship markup only - the CSS still has to be imported once.
      The frontmatter of the layout every page uses is a good spot. Import
      everything:
    </p>
    <Code
      code={`---
// src/layouts/Layout.astro
import "opui-css/css/imports.css"
---`}
      lang="astro"
    />
    <p>
      Or pick and choose in a CSS file, and import that file in the layout
      instead:
    </p>
    <Code
      code={`/* src/styles/global.css */\n${pickAndChooseCss}`}
      lang="css"
    />
    <Code
      code={`---
// src/layouts/Layout.astro
import "../styles/global.css"
---`}
      lang="astro"
    />
    <p>
      Import <code>layers.css</code> first and <code>utils.css</code> last, it holds
      <code>.ui-sr-only</code> and the motion classes. <code>choice.css</code> goes
      before <code>checkbox.css</code>, <code>radio.css</code> and <code
        >switch.css</code
      >. Import <code>opui-css/css/components.css</code> instead of single component
      files to get every component.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="usage">How to use</h2>
    <Code
      code={`---
import { Button } from "opui-css/astro"
---

<Button variant="filled">Click me</Button>`}
      lang="astro"
    />
    <p>
      Containers take parts, such as <code>CardHeader</code> and <code
        >DialogActions</code
      >. Other components take named slots for rich content, such as <code
        >end-text</code
      > on a <code>TextField</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <DocLink href="/guide/concepts">Concepts</DocLink> explains how props map to
      classes, the cascade layers and what needs JavaScript. Then browse the <DocLink
        href="/components">components</DocLink
      >. <DocLink href="/guide/theming">Theming</DocLink> covers colors, density,
      motion and contrast.
    </p>
  </section>
</Guide>
